他们很想听听你的故事，当人们崩溃时，你让人们发笑，但是关于你把剧本放在哪里、你是否在中间吃东西的任何事情？

00:01:21.439 --> 00:01:26.519
Just those little little fun facts that I think people would enjoy hearing Josh.
我认为人们会喜欢听到乔希的那些小有趣的事实。

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:31.980
Yeah, well key note address about You know what's it what's life like on a sitcom set?
是的，主题演讲是关于你知道情景喜剧片场的生活是什么样的吗？

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.834
I mean we're on stage 22 at the Fox lot in West LA.
我的意思是我们在西洛杉矶 Fox 场地的第 22 赛段。

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:52.459
It's it's a huge like aircraft hangar basically Um, if you look up, there's just, it looks like endless wood and beams and cross, you know, things in the sky and there's lights hanging from and yeah, hugely high ceiling.
这是一个巨大的飞机库，基本上，嗯，如果你抬头看，它看起来就像无尽的木头、横梁和十字架，你知道，天空中的东西，有灯光悬挂在，是的，非常高的天花板上。

00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:57.780
Um, probably, uh, yeah, not great for your allergies.
嗯，可能，呃，是的，对你的过敏不太好。

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:03.340
Um, but, um, there's like dust from Planet of the Apes and flying around in there.
嗯，但是，嗯，就像《猩球崛起》里的灰尘一样，在那里飞来飞去。

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.980
I think Planet of the Apes was out there.
我认为《猩球崛起》就在那里。

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:05.980
Yeah.
是的。

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.460
Some really classic old Hollywood movies were shot on that stage.
一些非常经典的好莱坞老电影就是在那个舞台上拍摄的。

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.460
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:17.340
Also, when you're on the Fox, if you drive in the front gate, you see the huge painted Simpsons mural.
此外，当您乘坐福克斯巴士时，如果您从前门开车，您会看到巨大的辛普森一家壁画。

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.939
There's, isn't Darth Vader and Luke Skywalker, there was a thing on there.
那里，不是达斯·维德和卢克·天行者，那里有一个东西。

00:02:22.939 --> 00:02:28.340
So you drive on to these lots and you feel like you're in old Hollywood kind of immediately.
所以当你开车到这些地段时，你会感觉自己立刻就到了老好莱坞。

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.099
It's really- And in the shadow of the die-hard building, also.
这真的是——而且还在顽固建筑的阴影下。

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:32.099
That's right.
这是正确的。

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:35.340
We looked up and saw the die-hard building for nine seasons.
我们抬头看到了九季的顽固建筑。

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:48.539
You know, there's a, there's a candy cart floating around that has like, like any candy you could ever imagine, but it also had a, uh, uh, uh, weren't there piles of scripts that if you needed a script, like the latest revision of the script?
你知道，有一个，有一辆糖果车漂浮在周围，里面有，就像你能想象到的任何糖果一样，但它也有，呃，呃，呃，不是有成堆的脚本，如果你需要一个脚本，比如最新版本的脚本吗？

00:02:48.539 --> 00:02:59.900
So I think like when you're on a show, especially if you're on camera, you have to train yourself, you cannot eat all the candy you want because you will look different by the end of the season than you did when you started.
所以我认为当你在节目中时，特别是当你在镜头前时，你必须训练自己，你不能吃掉所有你想吃的糖果，因为到季节结束时你看起来会与开始时不同。

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.460
It's really true.
这是真的。

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.280
I remember I would, I never liked carrying the whole script.
我记得我会的，我从来不喜欢携带整个剧本。

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.280
I would rip out the three pages, four pages of the scene.
我会把场景的三页、四页撕下来。

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.740
And I would rehearse them most of the time.
我大部分时间都会排练它们。

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:22.939
I was somewhat off book, sometimes I wasn't, but I would, sometimes if it was just a little, I would just isolate what my lines and I would have them.
我有点脱离书本，有时不是，但我会，有时如果只是一点点，我就会把我的台词隔离出来，然后我就会有它们。

00:03:22.939 --> 00:03:30.860
And then I would either, I'd put them under a prop on the desk, you know, like on a desk or a lot of pages underneath.
然后我要么把它们放在桌子上的一个支柱下，你知道，就像放在桌子上或下面的很多页面上。

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:38.699
I'm sure that a props and set dressing were just finding pages stuffed in couch cushions and behind pillows constantly.
我确信道具和布景只是不断地在沙发垫和枕头后面找到塞满的页面。

00:03:38.699 --> 00:03:41.180
Because you forget that you left them there, right?
因为你忘记了你把它们留在那里了，对吗？

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.419
I would have them in my back pocket.
我会把它们放在我的后口袋里。

00:03:42.419 --> 00:03:47.340
Sometimes wardrobe would have to come through and say, oh, your script's poking out, your back pocket.
有时，衣柜必须走过来说，哦，你的剧本露出来了，你的后口袋。

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:59.759
But the other thing that we would do, especially if there was a scene with all five of us, and what's weird is the more successful the show gets, the lazier the actors get.
但我们会做的另一件事，特别是如果有一个我们五个人的场景，奇怪的是演出越成功，演员就越懒。

00:03:59.759 --> 00:04:15.424
because you get better at doing it, you get better at, you get better at doing it, you get better at, you know your character, I mean, it's so hand in glove, you're just, you know how to play this character, you own the character, they know you own it.
因为你做得更好，你做得更好，你做得更好，你做得更好，你了解你的性格，我的意思是，它是如此紧密，你只是，你知道如何扮演这个角色，你拥有这个角色，他们知道你拥有它。

00:04:15.424 --> 00:04:21.765
So we had this wonderful script supervisor named Janet Kagan, who was British and sassy and hilarious.
所以我们有一位出色的剧本总监，名叫珍妮特·卡根（Janet Kagan），她是英国人，时髦又搞笑。

00:04:21.765 --> 00:04:25.246
And she was always right next to Pam behind the monitor.
她总是在监视器后面的帕姆旁边。

00:04:25.246 --> 00:04:33.700
And she marks up like where people got lime I'm strong or right or circles takes that Pam says, that's a good take and she'll circle it.
她会标记，就像人们在哪里得到了石灰，“我很坚强”或“正确”，或者帕姆说，这是一个很好的选择，她会圈出它。

00:04:33.699 --> 00:04:35.139
And it's a whole like code.
这是一个完整的代码。

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:38.980
She's got colored pencils and all sorts of stuff that I never understood.
她有彩色铅笔和各种我无法理解的东西。

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.540
But we would often gather around and Janet would run lines with us.
但我们经常聚集在一起，珍妮特会和我们一起排队。

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.300
And we would do that right before we shot.
我们会在拍摄之前这样做。

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:51.860
We would just gather around Janet's podium and learn the lines, you know, not always.
我们只是聚集在珍妮特的讲台周围，学台词，你知道，但并不总是如此。

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.379
Sometimes we would come in and we'd really have them.
有时我们会进来，我们真的会得到它们。

00:04:54.379 --> 00:04:57.379
But a lot of times you were learning as you went.
但很多时候你是边走边学的。

00:04:57.379 --> 00:05:05.740
And then the moment she was funny to witness because it would be like, you're acting and you're trying to get out of your workings and seeing it, working through the lines a little bit and Janet would be like eating a bowl of her puffins.
然后她见证的那一刻很有趣，因为这就像，你在表演，你试图摆脱你的工作并看到它，稍微完成台词，珍妮特就像在吃一碗她的海雀。

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.199
And just be like, what's the mean by breaking up?
只是想，分手意味着什么？

00:05:08.199 --> 00:05:09.100
And then just go back to it.
然后再回到它。

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.199
You should be doing that.
你应该这样做。

00:05:10.199 --> 00:05:21.060
It was also great to hear Janet, this British woman like reading Barney lines, like reading like the kind of gnarliest Barney lines in this thick British accent.
听到珍妮特也很高兴，这个英国女人喜欢读巴尼台词，喜欢用浓重的英国口音读最粗俗的巴尼台词。

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.139
It was really funny.
真的很有趣。

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:32.300
So yeah, I mean, it was always kind of, you know, I'd walk in and if we were there in the morning you kind of blaze through craft service and maybe grab some oatmeal and a cup of coffee.
所以，是的，我的意思是，你知道，我总是会走进去，如果我们早上在那里，你会享受手工服务，也许会买一些燕麦片和一杯咖啡。

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.339
And you ask him craft service like what's for lunch?
你问他工艺服务，比如午餐吃什么？

00:05:35.339 --> 00:05:36.819
You know, it's just rice.
你知道，这只是米饭。

00:05:36.819 --> 00:05:38.139
Breakfast rice.
早餐米饭。

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:40.579
We did often freak out about how much we love breakfast.
我们确实常常因为自己有多喜欢早餐而感到惊慌。

00:05:40.579 --> 00:05:41.420
Breakfast rice was good.
早餐米饭不错。

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.379
I think that was in the later seasons.
我想那是在后来的几季里。

00:05:43.379 --> 00:05:44.300
Yeah, it was.
是的，确实如此。

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.939
Yeah.
是的。

00:05:45.939 --> 00:05:47.980
But you know, it becomes your home away from home.
但你知道，它成为你的家外之家。

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.220
You know, you have your meals there.
你知道，你在那里吃饭。

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.259
You get to know the crew.
你会认识船员。

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:55.660
You get to know the crews, spouses and kids.
您会认识工作人员、配偶和孩子。

00:05:55.660 --> 00:06:07.139
And I don't know, I think that people, when they watch how I met your mother, I think I've said this before, they think it's five people, but it's 75 people.
我不知道，我认为人们，当他们看到我如何遇见你母亲时，我想我以前说过，他们认为是五个人，但实际上是 75 个人。

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:10.459
You know, the set is a buzz with people.
你知道，这个场景很受人们欢迎。

00:06:10.459 --> 00:06:19.100
And when in between scenes, people are coming along and they're fussing with your face and they're fussing with your hair and they're giving you a note and they're fussing with your collar.
在场景之间，人们走过来，他们对你的脸大惊小怪，他们对你的头发大惊小怪，他们给你一张纸条，他们对你的衣领大惊小怪。

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:24.100
You know, there's just a very active life going on on set.
你知道，片场的生活非常活跃。

00:06:25.779 --> 00:06:26.360
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:26.940
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:26.939 --> 00:06:30.740
And it really matters what that energy is of that life, what that kind of ecosystem is.
生命的能量是什么，生态系统是什么，这确实很重要。

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.139
And that's a lot of people bringing that energy.
有很多人带来了这种能量。

00:06:33.139 --> 00:06:39.980
And we just had an amazing, amazing crew that just had the warmest energy where everybody felt safe to do their best work.
我们拥有一支非常非常出色的团队，他们拥有最温暖的能量，让每个人都感到安全，可以尽自己最大的努力。

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:43.579
And it was fantastic, doesn't always happen.
这太棒了，但并不总是发生。

00:06:43.579 --> 00:06:45.019
A couple of things I could point out.
我可以指出一些事情。

