I did a show for NBC for a season called Rise, which was a really lovely show that Jason And I gave myself a challenge that I stuck to the entire time, which was I never brought my phone to set.
我为 NBC 做了一个名为《崛起》的节目，这是一个非常可爱的节目，杰森和我给自己提出了一个挑战，我一直坚持这个挑战，那就是我从来没有带手机去设置。

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:36.820
I would have it in my dressing room, I would check it when I had to go do a costume change or whatever.
我会把它放在更衣室里，当我必须去换服装或做其他事情时我会检查它。

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:40.500
I never once brought it set, but it was also when I was learning guitar.
我从来没有带过它，但也是在我学吉他的时候。

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:49.299
So I brought my guitar to set and we were often filming in this theater, this big auditorium that they actually built on a stage in Green Point in Brooklyn.
所以我把吉他带到了片场，我们经常在这个剧院拍摄，这个大礼堂实际上是在布鲁克林绿点的一个舞台上建造的。

00:08:49.299 --> 00:08:53.919
And I would sit in the audience and I would, you know, learn my lines, but I would noodle around on the guitar.
我会坐在观众席上，你知道，我会学习台词，但我会弹着吉他。

00:08:53.919 --> 00:09:03.220
I was learning how to finger pick and I'm pretty convinced giving myself those hours to play the guitar while not being on my own set.
我正在学习如何指弹，我非常确信给自己一些时间来弹吉他，而不是在自己的房间里。

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:08.340
It made me such a better guitar player and I think it made me a better actor, a more present actor on set.
它让我成为一个更好的吉他手，我认为它让我成为一个更好的演员，一个在片场更有表现力的演员。

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:10.940
So I tried to do that.
所以我尝试这样做。

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.299
The phone is a focus killer.
手机是焦点杀手。

00:09:14.299 --> 00:09:18.779
It's actually prohibits you from getting to know your cast members as well as you could.
它实际上阻止了你尽可能地了解你的演员。

00:09:18.779 --> 00:09:19.333
I agree.
我同意。

00:09:19.333 --> 00:09:20.302
It's not good.
这不好。

00:09:20.302 --> 00:09:21.962
We are all very seduced.
我们都很着迷。

